-- Runnable face-search queries: ./doris_sql.py sample_query.sql   (database: VELODB_DATABASE, see env.example)
-- The query vector is dataset face #5 (Lauren Bacall), ArcFace 512-d, L2-normalized.
--
--   * inner_product_approximate(...) + ORDER BY ... DESC LIMIT k is the shape the
--     HNSW index serves; inner_product(...) is the exact brute-force scan.
--   * Filter only on columns with an inverted index (gender, source, label_score_pct,
--     birth_year, age, photo_year). Any other predicate forces a brute-force scan.
--   * inverted_index_skip_threshold=100 makes Doris use the inverted index even for
--     broad predicates (default: skip it above 50% of rows, which also disables HNSW).
--   * Filters leaving < 30% of rows (ann_index_candidate_rows_percent_threshold)
--     are served by an exact scan of those rows: better recall than filtered HNSW.
-- Check which path ran: SET enable_profile = true, run the query, then look for
-- AnnIndexTopNSearchCnt (HNSW) vs AnnIndexFallbackBruteForceCnt in the profile.


